---
// Three worlds, one runtime — pitch section explaining gjsify's unique
// position: GNOME + Node.js + Web APIs fused in a single GJS process.
// Concrete example beats generic claim: a real browser game engine
// (Excalibur.js) runs natively in a Gtk.Window, with no embedded browser.
// Compared to Electron, this means no Chromium runtime to ship, no
// double process tree, and full Adwaita / GTK desktop integration.
---

<section class="fusion">
  <div class="fusion-inner">
    <p class="fusion-eyebrow">What makes GJSify different</p>
    <h2 class="fusion-title">Three worlds, one runtime</h2>
    <p class="fusion-lead">
      GNOME, Node.js, and the Web have lived in separate runtimes for a
      decade. GJSify dissolves the boundary — every API lands inside one
      SpiderMonkey process and shares the same memory, the same event
      loop, the same GTK main context.
    </p>

    <div class="fusion-stack" role="presentation">
      <div class="fusion-pillar fusion-pillar-gnome">
        <div class="fusion-pillar-head">
          <span class="fusion-pillar-tag">GNOME</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="fusion-pillar-list">
          <li>Gtk 4 widgets</li>
          <li>libadwaita</li>
          <li>GIO file / network / DBus</li>
          <li>GStreamer pipelines</li>
          <li>WebKit, libsoup, Cairo</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="fusion-pillar fusion-pillar-node">
        <div class="fusion-pillar-head">
          <span class="fusion-pillar-tag">Node.js</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="fusion-pillar-list">
          <li><code>fs</code> · <code>net</code> · <code>http(s)</code></li>
          <li><code>stream</code> · <code>events</code> · <code>process</code></li>
          <li><code>crypto</code> · <code>worker_threads</code></li>
          <li><code>util</code> · <code>buffer</code> · <code>url</code></li>
          <li>44 of the 50 stdlib modules</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="fusion-pillar fusion-pillar-web">
        <div class="fusion-pillar-head">
          <span class="fusion-pillar-tag">Web</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="fusion-pillar-list">
          <li><code>fetch</code> · <code>WebSocket</code> · SSE</li>
          <li><code>Canvas 2D</code> · WebGL · WebGPU bridge</li>
          <li>WebRTC · WebAudio · Gamepad</li>
          <li><code>FormData</code> · Streams · Crypto</li>
          <li>DOM events, Mutation / Resize observers</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="fusion-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="fusion-output">
        <div class="fusion-output-head">
          <span class="fusion-output-tag">GJSify</span>
        </div>
        <p class="fusion-output-text">
          One SpiderMonkey process. One TypeScript codebase. Zero glue
          between worlds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fusion-callout">
      <p class="fusion-callout-eyebrow">For example</p>
      <p class="fusion-callout-headline">
        Ship a browser game engine — without shipping a browser.
      </p>
      <p class="fusion-callout-body">
        <a href="https://excaliburjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Excalibur.js</a> renders directly into a <code>Gtk.GLArea</code> through GJSify's WebGL bridge.
        Pointer, keyboard, and gamepad input flows through GTK4 event controllers, dispatched as W3C DOM events.
        Audio runs on GStreamer through the Web Audio API. The whole game lives in one process — the same
        one that draws the Adwaita window around it. No <code>WebKit.WebView</code>, no IPC bridge, no
        embedded Chromium.
      </p>
      <div class="fusion-vs">
        <div class="fusion-vs-row">
          <span class="fusion-vs-label">Electron app</span>
          <span class="fusion-vs-value fusion-vs-bad">~150 MB Chromium runtime · separate renderer process · webContents bridge · X11/Wayland double-buffered</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fusion-vs-row">
          <span class="fusion-vs-label">GJSify app</span>
          <span class="fusion-vs-value fusion-vs-good">Stock GJS · single process · native GTK4 widgets · uses the GNOME runtime the user already has installed</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
  .fusion {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
    /* The pillar grid adapts to the actual content column (which varies with
       the two sidebars), not the viewport. */
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .fusion-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .fusion-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .fusion-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .fusion-lead {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.15rem);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* --- Pillar layout ---
     Three pillars side by side, then a downward arrow, then the GJSify
     output card across the full width — each element gets room to breathe
     instead of squeezing five columns into one row. */
  .fusion-stack {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    width: 100%;
    align-items: stretch;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .fusion-pillar,
  .fusion-output {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--adw-border-radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--adw-card-border);
    background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .fusion-pillar-head,
  .fusion-output-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .fusion-pillar-tag,
  .fusion-output-tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .fusion-pillar-gnome .fusion-pillar-tag { background: rgba(229, 165, 10, 0.18); color: #e5a50a; }
  .fusion-pillar-node  .fusion-pillar-tag { background: rgba(38, 162, 105, 0.18); color: #26a269; }
  .fusion-pillar-web   .fusion-pillar-tag { background: rgba(53, 132, 228, 0.18); color: var(--sl-color-accent); }
  .fusion-output-tag {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--sl-color-accent-high) 0%, var(--sl-color-accent) 60%, #9141ac 100%);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .fusion-pillar-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .fusion-pillar-list code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    white-space: nowrap; /* chips wrap between items, never inside a name */
  }

  .fusion-arrow {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    justify-self: center;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    display: flex;
    padding-block: 0.25rem;
  }

  .fusion-arrow svg {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
  }

  .fusion-output {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    text-align: center;
    border-color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--sl-color-accent-low), 0 8px 24px rgba(53, 132, 228, 0.18);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--sl-color-accent-low) 0%, var(--sl-color-bg-nav) 80%);
  }

  .fusion-output-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* --- Concrete-example callout --- */
  .fusion-callout {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    border-radius: var(--adw-border-radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--adw-card-border);
    background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .fusion-callout-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .fusion-callout-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .fusion-callout-body {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.4vw, 1rem);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }

  .fusion-callout-body a {
    color: var(--sl-color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .fusion-callout-body a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .fusion-vs {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--adw-card-border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .fusion-vs-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .fusion-vs-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .fusion-vs-value {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .fusion-vs-bad  { color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .fusion-vs-good { color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }

  /* --- Responsive ---
     Starlight's content column caps at 45rem (720px), so the pillars sit
     three-across inside it on desktop; only genuinely narrow layouts stack. */
  @container (max-width: 640px) {
    .fusion-stack {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .fusion-output {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .fusion-vs-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
